# Global excludes. `.claude/worktrees/` is where Claude Code puts the worktrees
# it creates, and it exposes no setting for the path. A nested worktree is a
# `.git` file plus a full checkout, so without this every repo shows an
# untracked `.claude/` the moment Claude Code creates one.
#
# `wt` and GitLens both create OUTSIDE the repo — `<parent>/<repo>.worktrees/`,
# see ~/.config/worktrunk/config.toml — so they need no entry here.
.claude/worktrees/
